;; The negative controls of repr/python's read and print checks (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a); doc/python/PY11-PREP.md's
;; R1; queue 212): per corpus a crossed pair of two files that pass every judge, the subject and the reference. After its
;; run each check judges the subject's output against the reference's expected result by its own judge, which must fail:
;; the round trip (bin/repr-python roundtrip: the subject's print, its helper's dump, by judge-file against the reference's
;; original; --text: the print's bytes and code, by judge-text), the token check (lex-check: the subject's native tokens by
;; judge-dump against the reference's tokdump) and the tree check (parse-check, and --full: the subject's native dump,
;; named as the reference, by judge-dump against the reference's pydump tree). "control passed:" or "control not judged:"
;; fails the check; a pair a selection (--only-list) did not run is printed as left (the gate's rotations keep both files
;; in every list: test/gate/crops/python.edn's :always). No control is a row of the results, the known files or the
;; counts (arbace.repr.python.results/judge-controls). Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id "samples" :corpus "samples" :subject "classes.py" :reference "functions.py"
  :why "two samples of other node classes: a class body against function definitions"}
 {:id "stdlib" :corpus "stdlib" :subject "Lib/keyword.py" :reference "Lib/colorsys.py"
  :why "two small plain modules (64 and 166 lines), neither in a known file"}
 {:id "lib-test" :corpus "lib-test" :subject "Lib/test/test_keyword.py" :reference "Lib/test/test_colorsys.py"
  :why "two small unittest modules (56 and 126 lines), the stdlib pair's tests"}
 {:id "site-packages" :corpus "site-packages" :subject "usr/lib/python3.14/site-packages/packaging/_structures.py"
  :reference "usr/lib/python3.14/site-packages/packaging/errors.py"
  :why "two pure-Python modules of packaging 26.3 (33 and 94 lines), the same on both architectures' apks"}
 {:id "lex-errors" :corpus "lex-errors" :subject "operators.py" :reference "prefixes-ft.py"
  :why "two of the tokenizer's cases that lex and parse (lex-check's and parse-check's corpus, not the round trips')"}]
